    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 624517835001856
    m_Localized: Come back anytime to continue restoring the artifact.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 626313739505664
    m_Localized: Are you sure you want to start a new game?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 626544380088320
    m_Localized: Your progress will be reset and cannot be recovered.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 626889151877120
    m_Localized: Confirm
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 632810972254208
    m_Localized: Language
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661625995923456
    m_Localized: Coin inscribed Chong Ning Tong Bao
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661675153166336
    m_Localized: "The characters on this coin exhibit Emperor Huizong\u2019s distinctive
      calligraphic style, known as \u201Cslender gold\u201D because it resembled
      finely spun filaments of the precious metal. Huizong made an effort to present
      himself as a man of cultivated tastes through various means. His writings were
      often carved in stone or metal, as here, and circulated widely among the public."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661711144488960
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s your first artifact, Nova.\nI hope this is a beautiful
      start to your journey here!\n\n- Ms. Maya :)"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661745072214016
    m_Localized: P.S Amazing to see this project in the hands of someone so competent!
      I know I can trust you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661833643331584
    m_Localized: Paperweight in the shape of a horse
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661993203044352
    m_Localized: "Cast in silver, this elegant standing horse may have served as
      a paperweight on a scholar\u2019s desk. The figure reflects both the refined
      metalwork and cultivated aesthetics valued by intellectuals of the period."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662160123760640
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s another Chinese artifact! A beauty... Something I would
      personally have in my house, to be honest :)\n\n- Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662186422046720
    m_Localized: "p.s So your mom is Tara Arkana? I\u2019ve heard of her from an
      excavation project back in the early 2000s... Her dedication to represent Indonesia
      internationally was so inspiring for me as a young historian back then!\n\n-
      Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662376306577408
    m_Localized: Jar with Dragon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662389711572992
    m_Localized: White porcelain painted with cobalt blue, a style that first flourished
      in China in the fourteenth century, is arguably the most important development
      in the history of ceramics. Commissioned by the court, this spectacular storage
      jar, made in the kilns in Jingdezhen, is dated to the rule of the Xuande emperor
      by an inscription on its shoulder. Its painted decoration features an animated
      dragon undulating across a sparsely clouded sky.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662411404513280
    m_Localized: 'Great job on the last one!


      Think you can handle this bigger
      artifact? You got this!


      - Ms. Maya :)'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662432128569344
    m_Localized: p.s So it is true! So were you born and raised in the Netherlands?
      I heard they have amazing museums there, including the museum we got these
      returned Indonesian artifacts from!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662504727777280
    m_Localized: Kendi
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662559601856512
    m_Localized: Kendi is a traditional water container often used for storing and
      drinking water. They may also serve ritual and ceremonial purposes. The term
      is derived from the Sanskrit word "kundika," which refers to a water vessel.
      This kendi is made from gold, dated from 8-9th century Central Javanese period
      in Indonesia.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662600655704064
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s your next artifact. Another Indonesian artifact! Take
      good care of this one, Nova :)\n\nGood luck!\n\n- Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662615998468096
    m_Localized: "p.s I want to make sure of something: did your mom really move
      to the Netherlands in the 80\u2019s for work? She always sounded so cool to
      me... Like, she\u2019s an Indonesian archeologist abroad when only a small
      amount of Indonesians were able to afford any kind of higher education back
      in her times!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662704598945792
    m_Localized: Kris
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662738652499968
    m_Localized: The kris, with its sinuous, snakelike blade, is the most characteristic
      weapon of Indonesia. Considered from early times to be imbued with great spiritual
      power, it is still an integral part of Indonesian culture.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662756914499584
    m_Localized: 'Your first Indonesian artifact here, Nova!


      Take great care
      of this one!


      - Ms. Maya'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662772081102848
    m_Localized: P.S So your mom was an archeologist? Her love for history definitely
      shows in you! How is she doing?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662827815014400
    m_Localized: Winged Scarab Amulet
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662876884176896
    m_Localized: 'This winged scarab consists of three pieces: an actual scarab beetle
      and two separately made wings. The wings are not those of a beetle, but those
      of a bird, as is apparent by their shape and the indication of individual feathers.
      Each piece features several small holes that were used to fasten the winged
      scarab to the wrappings of a mummy. Winged scarabs, meant to guarantee the
      rebirth of the deceased, were very popular funerary amulets.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662906575654912
    m_Localized: "Anyway, the latest pieces from Egypt just arrived...\n\nGood luck!
      \n\n-Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662950208999424
    m_Localized: "P.S I\u2019m so sorry about your mom\u2019s diagnosis yesterday...
      Glad to hear your aunt is there to help her out. \n\nIs there any way I can
      support you through this?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 670290119364608
    m_Localized: Replay
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 670376157122560
    m_Localized: Continue Story
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 671280864301056
    m_Localized: Peel off the sticky note...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 671435663478784
    m_Localized: Open the box and start restore...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681396854460416
    m_Localized: "Finally finished my first artifact in Indonesia! Kind of nervous
      at first, but Ms. Maya was so so sweet and supportive.\n\nCan\u2019t wait to
      tell Mama about this! I think she went to China for an excavation project once...?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681702430478336
    m_Localized: "The artifact this time is a horse-shaped paperweight. I agree with
      Ms. Maya, this is something I would love to have at home :D\n\nAnyways, I chatted
      a little about Mama with Ms. Maya and found out that she is THAT famous in
      the Indonesian history scene...? I keep feeling prouder and prouder of her.
      I\u2019ll tell her that when I call tonight :) Hope that can help her feel
      better."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681728636489728
    m_Localized: "The artifact this time is a jar and I think I\u2019ve always loved
      this type of design on ceramics! Had a lot of fun on this one.\n\nAlso, it\u2019s
      so interesting that me and Ms. Maya keep having these small conversations.
      I truly appreciate her effort to connect with me even though she\u2019s always
      so, so busy. I\u2019m glad I share this interest of history with someone that
      knows Mama too..."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681751302508544
    m_Localized: 'Got another Indonesian artifact! It was so, so shiny with pretty
      carvings... I LOVE how pretty it looked. Can totally understand how Mama fell
      in love with them and wanted to share it with the world so badly.


      Also!
      Just truly realized how cool Mama was for being an Indonesian archeologist
      working abroad in the 80s. I distinctly remember begging Mama to go with her
      on excavation trips but she would only take me to ones within the Netherlands...'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681772164976640
    m_Localized: "My very first Delft-returned Indonesian artifact today. Big day
      for me and Mama :) \nI hope this lifts her spirit, seeing her dream come true
      through me.\n\nAnyways I need to call Mama right after I get back home. My
      aunt haven\u2019t gotten back to me since she went with Mama for her check
      up at the hospital..."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681785788076032
    m_Localized: "Got my hands on an Egyptian artefact today! Reminds me of those
      days where I used to be obsessed with the entire ancient Egyptian civilization...\n\nOn
      the other hand, I still can\u2019t believe she got diagnosed with that yesterday.
      I wish I could be there with her but she keeps insisting that doing this project
      for her is the best way I can help her... Thank goodness Auntie is there to
      accompany her."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 684852990316544
    m_Localized: 'To-do List:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
